<td>Robotic tone, native errors</td>
<td>Approved by native speaker</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Creative</td>
<td>Imagery, colors, holidays</td>
<td>Aligned with local culture</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Payment</td>
<td>Method coverage</td>
<td>TOP 3 local methods available</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Compliance</td>
<td>Regulatory risk</td>
<td>No violations recorded</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Channels</td>
<td>Platform selection, timing</td>
<td>ROI above market average</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<hr />
<h2>Final Thought</h2>
<p>Localization isn't a one-time task—it requires <strong>continuous optimization</strong>. Set a weekly review to correlate user feedback and conversion data with localization issues. Only then will your budget truly hit the mark.</p>
